# subsystems to DISABLE.

# Wireless (802.11) — DELIBERATELY RE-ENABLED 2026-08-03
#
# Wi-Fi is now ON by choice: the device needs wireless networking. This weakens
# the hardening posture (the 802.11 stack is a large, network-facing attack
# surface) and is a deliberate trade-off, not an oversight.
#
# To turn Wi-Fi back OFF, change the four "##" markers below back to "#".
# The directives are disabled rather than deleted so the hard-won knowledge here
# is not lost — parse_disabled_symbols() in scripts/lib.sh only recognises lines
# starting exactly "# CONFIG_", so "##" makes it skip them.
#
# KEEP THIS NOTE: disabling CONFIG_WIRELESS alone is NOT enough. The Wi-Fi
# *drivers* under CONFIG_WLAN (b43, ath9k, ...) `select CFG80211`, and
# `make olddefconfig` then forces the wireless stack back ON. You must also
# disable the driver umbrella (WLAN) and the stack symbols (CFG80211/MAC80211)
# that get re-selected. With the drivers gone, nothing selects the stack and the
# disables finally stick. This cost a full rebuild to discover.
##  CONFIG_WIRELESS is not set
##  CONFIG_WLAN is not set
##  CONFIG_CFG80211 is not set
##  CONFIG_MAC80211 is not set

# Bluetooth
# CONFIG_BT is not set

# Sound — DELIBERATELY RE-ENABLED 2026-08-05
#
# CONFIG_SOUND is now ON by necessity, not choice. It broke the display, not
# just audio:
#
#   config DRM_VC4
#       depends on SND && SND_SOC
#       select SND_PCM
#       select SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC
#       ...
#
# (drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/Kconfig). vc4 — the driver for the ACTUAL display
# pipeline (HVS/HDMI/KMS) — has a HARD `depends on SND && SND_SOC`, because
# HDMI carries audio and vc4's HDMI encoder registers an ALSA codec as part of
# bringing up video at all. With CONFIG_SOUND=n cascading to SND=n, `make
# olddefconfig` could not force sound back on to satisfy the dependency (unlike
# the WLAN/CFG80211 case below) — it silently dropped DRM_VC4 from the config
# instead. Confirmed on-device: the compiled /boot/config-* had no DRM_VC4 line
# AT ALL (not even "# CONFIG_DRM_VC4 is not set" — a symbol whose dependencies
# can't be met is omitted entirely, not just turned off). v3d (3D/render-only,
# no display capability) still loaded fine, so `ip a`/`uname -r` looked normal
# and the Pi booted — Phosh's compositor just found zero connector-capable GPUs
# and crash-looped (`phoc-wlroots-CRITICAL: Found 0 GPUs, cannot create
# backend`), which greetd surfaced as a black screen with a blinking cursor and
# no visible error. Cost a full flash-and-boot cycle to diagnose.
#
# Same class of bug as the WLAN/CFG80211 trap below (a hardening disable
# tripping an unrelated `select`/`depends on` elsewhere in the tree), just
# running in the opposite direction (starves a dependency instead of getting
# re-selected) and landing on video instead of network. Same lesson: verify
# the *compiled* .config after any subsystem disable, not just that the fragment
# applied — see scripts/verify-disabled.sh (it reads the compiled config out of
# the built .apk for exactly this reason).
#
# Real trade-off, same as Wi-Fi: DRM_VC4's own `select`s force SND_PCM and
# SND_SOC_HDMI_CODEC on regardless, so as long as this device has a working
# HDMI display, some /dev/snd (HDMI audio out) will exist — that is not
# separable from having video on this SoC without patching vc4 itself. What
# IS still avoidable: standalone sound hardware vc4 does NOT need. Narrow that
# separately (e.g. `# CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO is not set` to stop arbitrary
# plugged-in USB audio devices) and verify each addition doesn't re-trip this
# same trap before trusting it.
##  CONFIG_SOUND is not set

# Module symbol versioning (MODVERSIONS)
# Not a subsystem — a build-cost and surface reduction. With MODVERSIONS on, the
# kernel build preprocesses every module source a SECOND time
# ("gcc -E -D__GENKSYMS__ ... | genksyms") purely to compute symbol-version CRCs.
# Observed live: every sampled cc1 during a build was one of these passes.
#
# Its only purpose is letting out-of-tree modules be version-checked against this
# kernel — and we dropped the linux-rpi-dev subpackage, so out-of-tree modules
# can't be built against it anyway. We pay the cost for a capability the design
# already forgoes. Expect roughly 15-25% off the kernel build (an -E pass is
# cheaper than a full compile, so this is not a halving).
# CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is not set
